{"answer": "C", "estimate": 2, "mechanism": "D", "confidence": 98, "reasoning": "Go allocates a minimum stack of 2 KB (_StackMin = 2048 bytes) for each newly spawned goroutine. Stack memory grows contiguously on demand when function frames require more space. Since these goroutines block immediately without deep call frames, each retains its initial 2 KB stack allocation."}
