{"answer": "B", "estimate": 256, "mechanism": "C", "confidence": 95, "reasoning": "Go shrinks stacks during garbage collection. In each GC cycle, if a goroutine uses less than 1/4 of its allocated stack, the runtime halves the stack size (copystack). After two GC cycles, the stack is halved twice, reducing it to approximately 1/4 of its peak size (~256 KB from ~1 MB)."}
